From: Ajay Kumar Nandam <ajay.nandam@oss.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: lpass-{tx,va}-macro: take the erhai v0.7.2 drivers

Replace lpass-tx-macro.c and lpass-va-macro.c with the files of
erhai-v0.7.2 and drop their PM_CLK dependency as erhai does. The kernel 3
series carried the earlier "switch to PM clock framework for runtime PM"
versions; erhai moved on to the FROMLIST "manage clocks in runtime PM"
versions, which enable macro, dcodec, mclk, npl and fsgen explicitly, and
adds HPF cut-off controls for the TX decimators (used by the UCM).

On OPD2413 with the PM-clock versions, microphone capture returns
full-scale garbage (~30000 zero crossings per second, almost unchanged
when the ADC and decimator gains are lowered by 28 dB).

erhai commits on these files, oldest first (authors as recorded there):
  bc29c081e yzddmr6: ASoC: codecs: lpass-tx-macro: add HPF cut-off controls for the decimators
  c11156217 Ajay Kumar Nandam: ASoC: codecs: lpass-va-macro: Switch to PM clock framework for runtime PM
  b723cd554 Ajay Kumar Nandam: ASoC: codecs: lpass-tx-macro: switch to PM clock framework for runtime PM
  d4f6a79ba Ajay Kumar Nandam: ASoC: codecs: lpass-{tx,rx}-macro: check clk_set_rate() return value
  75cf773ca Noahcdls: ASoC: codecs: lpass-macro: force runtime suspend across system sleep
  a7b7b0818 yzddmr6: Revert forced LPASS system suspend for resume isolation
  431d7ce0f yzddmr6: clk: qcom: gcc-sm8750: retain PCIe power while isolating resume resets
  9ead6de36 Ajay Kumar Nandam: FROMLIST: ASoC: codecs: lpass-tx-macro: manage clocks in runtime PM
  385a9a869 Ajay Kumar Nandam: FROMLIST: ASoC: codecs: lpass-va-macro: manage clocks in runtime PM
  f09e9e8f6 yzddmr6: ASoC: codecs: lpass: remove unused TX and VA PM clock dependencies (Kconfig)

[opd2413: files taken whole from erhai-v0.7.2; From: names the author of
 the two FROMLIST commits that change the clock handling.]
